    "result_text": "The build is green. Both tests pass \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it exercises both requirements.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for `POST /api/owners` following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions in the codebase:\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this makes the field both settable on input and returned on output. The `date` format makes the generated DTO use `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 Added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field with its column mapping, getter/setter, and a small single-responsibility `@PrePersist` callback (`defaultRegistrationDate`) that sets the date to `LocalDate.now()` only when none was supplied. This keeps the defaulting rule next to the field it governs and fires exactly once at creation, leaving a client-supplied date untouched.\n\n3. **Schemas** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four DB schema files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql).\n\nMapStruct's convention-based mapping picks up the new field automatically in both directions (`toOwner` and `toOwnerDto`), so no mapper or controller changes were needed \u2014 mirroring how the existing derived `initials` field flows through.\n\nBoth acceptance checkpoints pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted date \u2192 server's current date) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` preserved).",
